# Component Structure Rules

## Component Organization
- One component per file
- Component name must match file name
- Use functional components with hooks
- Keep components small and focused (single responsibility)

## Component Structure Pattern
```javascript
// UserProfile.jsx
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import PropTypes from 'prop-types';

/**
 * UserProfile component displays user information
 * @param {Object} props - Component props
 * @param {string} props.userId - User ID
 * @param {Function} props.onUpdate - Callback when user updates
 */
const UserProfile = ({ userId, onUpdate }) => {
  const [user, setUser] = useState(null);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);

  useEffect(() => {
    // Fetch user data
    fetchUser(userId).then(setUser).finally(() => setLoading(false));
  }, [userId]);

  if (loading) return <div>Loading...</div>;
  if (!user) return <div>User not found</div>;

  return (
    <div className="user-profile">
      {/* Component JSX */}
    </div>
  );
};

UserProfile.propTypes = {
  userId: PropTypes.string.isRequired,
  onUpdate: PropTypes.func
};

export default UserProfile;
```

## File Naming
- Components: PascalCase - `UserProfile.jsx`, `ProductCard.tsx`
- Utilities: camelCase - `formatDate.js`, `apiClient.js`
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE - `API_BASE_URL.js`

## Directory Structure
```
src/
├── components/      # Reusable components
├── pages/          # Page components
├── hooks/          # Custom hooks
├── utils/          # Utility functions
├── services/       # API services
├── context/        # React context
└── styles/         # CSS/styled components
```

## Hooks
- Use custom hooks for reusable logic
- Keep hooks focused on single responsibility
- Name hooks starting with "use": `useUserData`, `useApiCall`

## State Management
- Use useState for local component state
- Use useContext for shared state
- Use Redux/Zustand for global state (if needed)
- Avoid prop drilling - use context or state management
